course: dictionary
lesson: 767
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. «Bean» can mean a seed you can eat, the plant it grows on, or the seed of plants like coffee or cocoa. The words around it show you which meaning the writer means.
explain: Look at the context first. «Farmers cut the pods, scoop out the beans...» The pods and the farm tell you that beans here are seeds. If you are stuck, read the sentence again and ask: which meaning fits?
explain: Some phrases mean something different from the single words. «Full of beans» does not mean you have beans inside you; it means full of energy. «Spill the beans» means tell a secret. Learn these phrases as a whole.
fact: «Bean» can be a noun: a seed you can eat, which grows in a pod.
fact: A bean can also be the plant the seed grows on, like the beans in a school vegetable patch.
fact: Coffee beans and cocoa beans are seeds of other plants, used for food or drinks.
fact: «Full of beans» means full of energy. «Spill the beans» means tell a secret.
fact: As a verb, bean is informal and means to hit someone on the head.
exercise: «Deer droppings look like dark beans.» In this sentence, what does bean mean? | A plant growing in a garden | Energy | *A small dark shape, like a seed | A secret
exercise: «Mia was full of beans at the party.» What does full of beans mean? | *Full of energy | Tired and sleepy | Hungry for food | Covered in beans
exercise: «Please don't spill the beans about the surprise party!» What does spill the beans mean? | Hit someone on the head | Drop the food on the floor | *Tell a secret | Plant a seed
test: «Farmers scoop out the beans from the pods.» In this sentence, what are the beans? | A bump on the head | A secret | A tin of food | *Seeds inside the pods
test: «The ball beaned him on the head.» What does beaned mean? | Caught neatly | Kicked gently | *Hit on the head | Dropped quietly
exam: In which sentence does bean mean a seed you can eat? | «He was full of beans at breakfast.» | *«Once you plant beans, you have to water them and guard them.» | «She spilled the beans about the trip.» | «The ball beaned him.»
